# A PROFILE A SPLINE CAN ACTUALLY BE PART OF (M18).
#
# Before M18 the tangency below was refused outright, so the spline met the
# line with a visible kink -- and the solid built from it had the kink too,
# because the kernel was choosing its own end condition.

sketch Blade

tool line
click 0 0
click 120 0

tool spline
click 120 0
click 150 35
click 120 70
click 60 80
finish

# The spline's first click landed on the line's end, so the tool ALREADY
# inferred the coincidence -- and the line's first click landed on the origin,
# so that Fix is inferred too. Adding either by hand would be a second copy of
# a constraint that is already there, and the solver would rightly call the
# sketch redundant.
#
# What is NOT inferred is the tangency: nothing can guess that a curve meeting
# a line was meant to meet it smoothly.
constrain tangent Spline1 Line1

constrain horizontal Line1
dimension length Line1 120 as Root

solve

echo --- what did we build? ---
measure Line1
measure Spline1
measure Line1.start Spline1.end
